<App title="Lesson 2 — Hexatonic means six notes">
  <h1>Lesson 2 — Hexatonic means six notes</h1>
  <p>That’s all the word means. “Hexa” = six.</p>
  <p>The full G major scale has seven notes: G A B C D E F#. Over the C chord in a G-C-D-Em song, that F# sounds sour — it clashes with the chord underneath it.</p>
  <p>Leave F# out and you can’t hit a wrong note anymore. Six notes left:</p>
  <p style="font-size:22px;font-weight:600">G A B C D E</p>
  <p>This is the <strong>major hexatonic</strong>: scale degrees 1 2 3 4 5 6. Two ways to think about the same six notes:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Major pentatonic (the five-note shape you may already know) plus the 4th</li>
    <li>Major scale minus the 7th</li>
  </ul>

